details.returned_prompt:
{
  "high_level_description": "An editorial outdoor photograph of a late-afternoon lakeside camp on a northern England fell, with two down sleeping bags unrolled on the grass beside an open dome tent, rolling heather-streaked fells and a distant glacial lake receding into haze, shot on 35mm with Kodak Portra grain.",
  "compositional_deconstruction": {
    "background": "A northern England fellside in late afternoon. Rolling green fells rise in soft layers across the upper half of the frame, slopes streaked with purple-brown heather fading into atmospheric haze toward the horizon. Through a gap between the fells at upper right, a narrow ribbon of silver glacial water glints faintly. Cool-leaning natural daylight rakes in from the right at a low angle, casting gentle directional shadows across the grassy foreground. The grass underfoot is short and uneven, lit warmly from the right and cool in the shadowed patches.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Open dome tent in the middle ground just behind the sleeping bags, slightly right of center. Dark forest-green flysheet stretched over two crossing poles, mesh door flap tied back to one side revealing a grey foam mat and a crumpled cream wool blanket inside."
      },
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Battered canvas rucksack tipped on its side at the right edge of the campsite, midground. Faded olive-tan canvas with dark leather straps and brass buckles, top flap loose, contents partially visible. Beside it, a pair of worn brown leather hiking boots with scuffed toes and dusty laces, standing upright."
      },
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Mummy-shaped three-season down sleeping bag in muted sage green, laid out flat on the grass in the center-foreground at a slight diagonal, sharp focus. Partially unzipped along its length, hood bunched near the far end, soft puffy baffles catching the warm side light from the right."
      },
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Larger winter-weight down sleeping bag in deep charcoal, rolled loose beside the sage bag in the lower-center foreground, sharp focus. Thicker loft than the sage bag, heavier quilted paneling visible along its length, fabric reading as dense matte black-grey."
      },
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Enamel mug of tea resting on a flat grey stone next to the sage sleeping bag, left of center in the foreground. White enamel body with a chipped blue rim, dark tea visible inside, a faint curl of pale vapor rising from the surface."
      },
      {
        "type": "obj",
        "desc": "Out-of-focus tuft of grass in the lower-left foreground with a single small white wildflower, five delicate petals on a thin green stem, softly blurred."
      }
    ]
  }
}
